 "version": 1,
 "title": "Glitch Loop",
 "category": "Drums and grooves",
 "text": "Sound: a broken, glitchy machine loop: kick and snare under a spray of sixteenth-note noise hits, each one a different random colour, crushed. It plays by itself.\n\nHow it's built: one Clock at 126. Kick (steps 1, 4, 7 of a Sequencer on eighths) and snare (3 and 7). The glitch: noise through a band-pass whose CUTOFF a Sample & Hold sets to a new random place on every 1/16, struck by a short envelope on the same tick, then Crushed.\n\nTweak: the glitch filter's CV (how far the colours jump) and RESONANCE, the Crusher's BITS and RATE, TEMPO.",
